-- title:
--   Local Atkin–Lehner element for an Eichler order at ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q,q'$ be primes such that $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the algebra $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has all its nonzero elements invertible precisely when $q\in v$ or $q'\in v$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ and $N\in\mathbb{N}$ with `IsEichlerOrder R N`, i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two submodules satisfying `IsOrder` and maximal for $\le$ among such, with the index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ as additive groups equal to $N$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\neq q'$ and $\ell\nmid N$, and let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $\ell$. Write $R_v=$ [`Submodule.localBox R v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40), the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in R$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_v$. Then there is a unit $w$ of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ with: $w\in R_v$, $\ell w^{-1}\in R_v$, $w^{-1}\notin R_v$ and $\ell^{-1}w\notin R_v$ (multiplication by the images of $\ell$ and $\ell^{-1}$ under $\mathbb{Q}\to\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$); the same two membership statements for the $\mathbb{Q}$-scalar actions $\ell\cdot w^{-1}\in R_v$ and $\ell^{-1}\cdot w\notin R_v$; $w^2=\ell$; and, for every additive subgroup $O'$ characterised by $x\in O'\iff w^{-1}xw\in R_v$, the index of $R_v\cap O'$ in $R_v$ equals $\ell$.
--
--   This is the local Atkin–Lehner (uniformiser) element at a prime $\ell$ away from the ramification of $\mathbb{H}$ and from the Eichler level $N$: at such $\ell$ the completed algebra is split, the completed order is conjugate to $M_2(\mathbb{Z}_\ell)$, and $w$ normalises it up to an index-$\ell$ overlap. It feeds the level-raising step [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_finiteIdele_meetOrder_isEichlerOrder_mul_of_not_dvd_of_isIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_finiteIdele_meetOrder_isEichlerOrder_mul_of_not_dvd_of_isIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt), which passes from an Eichler order of level $N$ to one of level $N\ell$.
